        <definition>std::vector&lt;std::vector&lt;std::pair&lt;std::string, std::string&gt; &gt; &gt; AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::passes</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>passes</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::passes</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Draw the component once per entry, each with :cpp:member:`lines` and that entry&apos;s own lines
after them -- a source pass whose draws split by state, eg. a see-through layer blended where
the stencil marks a body behind it and drawn opaque everywhere else. **Default**: empty, one
draw with :cpp:member:`lines`
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="191" column="25" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="191" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1a2afae4bfae7cf4988ecd8c7e8c23ea0a" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; std::string &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::passPs</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>passPs</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::passPs</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Per entry of :cpp:member:`passes`, the HLSL that pass draws with in place of :cpp:member:`ps`
-- a source that draws one component with two shaders, eg. a solid one where the part is opaque
and a see-through one over a body. An empty entry, or none, keeps :cpp:member:`ps`. Each is
written beside :cpp:member:`ps` as a file of its own. **Default**: empty
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="202" column="25" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="202" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1a97dc20e0315e46bb34c998e54ea721a6" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>std::string AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::onlyWith</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>onlyWith</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::onlyWith</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
An output register (eg. ``&quot;o3&quot;``) a pass has to bind for the shader to draw there; a pass
that leaves it unbound (a depth pre-pass) draws the component with the game&apos;s own shader, as
any other component. Empty, the shader draws on every pass of the slot. **Default**: ``&quot;&quot;``
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="265" column="25" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="265" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1a9c6af9268cb9c803a08432d3db27c734" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::yieldToRabbitFX</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>yieldToRabbitFX</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::yieldToRabbitFX</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= false</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
A mod whose sections for the component hand its maps to RabbitFX keeps the target slot&apos;s GAME
shader there: RabbitFX works by patching the game&apos;s shaders, never this one, so a RabbitFX mod
drawn with it loses its effect (a mod&apos;s robotic legs drawn as skin). **Default**: ``false``
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="275" column="18" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="275" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1a64fc798f150c19250d203acd7b2bc269" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; <ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_binding" kindref="compound">Binding</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;Binding&gt; AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::registers</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>registers</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::registers</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Bindings the component takes only while this shader draws it, after the plan entry&apos;s own --
a register (or a register&apos;s role) the shader reads in the SOURCE&apos;s layout. With
:cpp:member:`yieldToRabbitFX`, a mod that keeps the target&apos;s shader keeps the plan&apos;s
bindings alone. **Default**: empty
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="286" column="25" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="286" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1a925fa2b98a7c1bedf5d1b88a129bde15" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::optional&lt; <ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_fixer_config_1_1_shader_1_1_after" kindref="compound">After</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::optional&lt;After&gt; AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::after</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>after</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::WWMIFixerConfig::Shader::after</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Draw the component only AFTER another component&apos;s draws in the same pass, whichever
order the game draws the two slots in.

The game does not keep one order: Lynae&apos;s jacket slot draws after her upper body in the
character menu and BEFORE it in the overworld. A see-through layer blends over whatever
is under it when it draws, so drawn first it blends over her hair and the scene behind
her -- and her body, drawn after, loses the depth test under it. Set, the component&apos;s
draw on a pass binding :cpp:member:`After::target` is held back when the other
component has not drawn yet, and made after that component&apos;s last draw instead.
**Default**: none, drawn where its slot draws
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" line="303" column="27" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/data/IniFixData/WWMIFixer.h" bodystart="303" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
A pixel shader a :cpp:struct:`SourceComponent` is drawn with in place of the target slot&apos;s
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

The fix writes the shader and its constant buffers beside the mod&apos;s buffers, declares
them in its own block (so an undo removes them), and turns each rerouted
``drawindexed`` of the component into a ``run =`` of a ``CustomShader`` section that binds
them and makes that draw. Everything the shader does not bind itself is the target
draw&apos;s: its vertex shader, its render targets and the textures the component&apos;s
:cpp:member:`plan` entry binds
</verbatim> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
